<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch Dec CPI seen flat at 2.3 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch Dec CPI seen flat at 2.3 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters expect the Dutch December consumer price index to drop 0.3 percent in December from November, leaving the year-on-year inflation rate unchanged at 2.3 percent.</p>
<p>December CPI is due on Friday morning. Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p> GMT   Date  Period   Indicator     Consensus  Range	Pvs</p>
<p> 0930  17/1  Dec	CPI mth/mth   -0.3 pct   -0.2/-0.4  -0.1</p>
<p> 0930  17/1  Dec	CPI yr/yr     +2.3 pct   +2.2/+2.6  +2.3</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, Generale Bank, MeesPierson, J.P. Morgan, NIBStrating and Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Kelly, Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
